# EAS Build's file uploader chokes on the kill-ai-slop skill's symlink
# (.claude/skills/kill-ai-slop -> .agents/skills/kill-ai-slop) — neither
# directory is part of the app itself, so just skip them for the build
# upload.
.agents
.claude

# The local android/ directory (generated by `expo prebuild` on this
# Windows machine) bakes in absolute Windows paths in a few places — e.g.
# react-native-nitro-modules' autolinked settings.gradle references
# "C:/push_up_counter/node_modules/...". EAS Build detects a checked-in
# android/ and uses it verbatim instead of running its own prebuild, so
# those Windows paths shipped straight to the Linux build image and broke
# Gradle project resolution. Excluding the whole directory makes EAS run
# prebuild itself, generating clean Linux-relative paths.
android
